     BackFaceColor->RGBColor[0.85, 0.45, 0.2],
     GraphicsColor->RGBColor[0.85, 0.45, 0.2],
     FontSize->12,
     FontColor->RGBColor[0.85, 0.45, 0.2]], {2.5, 0.15}], InsetBox[
    StyleBox["\<\"exclusivity ceiling (no-signaling)\"\>",
     StripOnInput->False,
     LineColor->GrayLevel[0.5],
     FrontFaceColor->GrayLevel[0.5],
     BackFaceColor->GrayLevel[0.5],
     GraphicsColor->GrayLevel[0.5],
     FontSize->8,
     FontColor->GrayLevel[0.5]], {2.5, -0.15}], InsetBox[
    StyleBox["\<\"quantum zone\"\>",
     StripOnInput->False,
     LineColor->RGBColor[0.2, 0.45, 0.85],
     FrontFaceColor->RGBColor[0.2, 0.45, 0.85],
     BackFaceColor->RGBColor[0.2, 0.45, 0.85],
     GraphicsColor->RGBColor[0.2, 0.45, 0.85],
     FontSize->9,
     FontColor->RGBColor[0.2, 0.45, 0.85]], {2.118033988749895, 0.3}], 
   InsetBox[
    StyleBox["\<\"'meta-optics' overhang\"\>",
     StripOnInput->False,
     LineColor->RGBColor[0.85, 0.45, 0.2],
     FrontFaceColor->RGBColor[0.85, 0.45, 0.2],
     BackFaceColor->RGBColor[0.85, 0.45, 0.2],
     GraphicsColor->RGBColor[0.85, 0.45, 0.2],
     FontSize->9,
     FontColor->RGBColor[0.85, 0.45, 0.2]], {2.368033988749895, 0.3}]},
  AspectRatio->0.3,
  ImageSize->580,
  PlotRange->{{1.8, 2.72}, {-0.28, 0.42}}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.9930477052329807`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[736]=",ExpressionUUID->"9ac48a57-8d7a-3c45-8740-bf3629dd3b4c"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
Sqrt[5] is the pentagon's analogue of the Tsirelson bound: the most a genuine \
quantum device can score. 5/2 is its analogue of the no-signaling ceiling: \
the most reachable while still respecting no-disturbance. The strip between \
them \[LongDash] the 'meta-optics' overhang \[LongDash] is the adversary's \
room, and it is the territory this whole project is built to survey.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"182a2011-8a1f-7942-8919-671511ff59c7"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Map of the Work \[LongDash] Objectives, Stages, and Verified Numbers", \
"Section",ExpressionUUID->"090b67f9-f0aa-1a47-bbc5-b8c04f03afd1"],

Cell["\<\
O1 correlation-based classification of statistics \[Rule] Stages 1-2, 4 \
(GE-001, CF-001..004).
O2 Lie-algebraic resource scaling \[Rule] Stages 5-6 (LP-002).
O3 conditions for indistinguishability \[Rule] Stages 3-4 (BBT-002, BBT-004).
O4 Hawking illustration \[Rule] The Cherry on Top (HK-003, HK-006, HK-007).
O5 signaling / communication feasibility \[Rule] Stage 13 (SIG-001..003).
Priority: AB-sheaf derivation of the composed bound \[Rule] Stage 12 \
(ESSAY-005, SH-006).
D1: GE copies vs \[Theta](G) \[Rule] Stages 10-11 (GE-002..004, ERG-003).
MESH: pentagon gluing \[Rule] Stages 7-8 (MESH-001..009, CERT-001..002).
MBQC: cluster-state realization \[Rule] Stage 9 (MESH-007..008, LP-003).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8d6cea73-8a86-1240-b2fa-9be0ad96542c"],

Cell["\<\
Results at a glance (every number kernel-verified in a module):
Classical 2 < quantum \[Sqrt]5 = 2.2360679775 < NCHV 5/2 (GE-001); contextual \
fraction 2\[Sqrt]5 - 4 = 0.4721.
Gluing limit densities: trans tau* = 1.3767177459, cis = 3/2; best word \
(cct)^inf gap 0.0698975 per block, beating pure-trans by 61%.
Epsilon-certificate ladder Gamma_7..Gamma_10 = 0.0770206, 0.0752664, \
0.0720260, 0.0714575, bracketing gap(cct).
Catalysis: \[Omega](C9^v3) = 8 proven; \[Omega](C9 v C9 v C9 v C5) \
\[GreaterEqual] 17 (17-clique witness, family [1,3,5,5,3]).
Geometric lens: single so(3) generator DLA = 1 (leaf) vs full cascade DLA = 3 \
(sphere); CV Hawking generator DLA = 10 = sp(4,R), active.
Signaling: SF(C5, quantum) = 2\[Sqrt]5 - 4 bits per round.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6ed78287-11ba-eb44-81fe-9547f27ae1bf"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Part I \[LongDash] The Atom and the Two-Lens Certificate", "Chapter",ExpressionUUID->"a79a4fb1-a6b2-d244-ba1e-b5ee394b8124"],

Cell["\<\
The central question, the KCBS-pentagon atom, and the two lenses that certify \
it: the correlation lens (the three-number ruler \[Alpha], \[Theta], \
\[Alpha]*) and the geometric lens (the dynamical Lie algebra), joined by the \
black-box protocol and its constructive mirror, the optical compiler. \
Modules: Stages 0-6. Objectives O1, O2, O3; tracks D2, BBT, EMU.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0e24ec4e-42e5-264e-9250-78f3dfb65e94"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Stage 0 \[LongDash] The Question: The Sealed Box", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"fb1f35a4-e379-a54f-a25d-9366bb9c94d2"],

Cell["\<\
Imagine a sealed box with some inputs and outputs. It behaves in ways that \
look quantum: its outputs show correlations no ordinary classical device \
should be able to produce. Can you ever be completely certain it is genuinely \
quantum, just by watching what goes in and out, without opening it \
\[LongDash] or could a clever engineer build a purely classical fake that \
produces the exact same numbers? That is the founding question, and the \
honest starting picture has two possible interiors behind one identical \
stream of clicks.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2da1ecd2-754a-224e-b7ca-6011d724d231"],

Cell["\<\
A device you can only poke from outside: same clicks, two candidate interiors:\
\>", "CodeText",ExpressionUUID->"5d6c4dc9-6bab-564a-9d96-d413f352b0d7"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Module[{bx, navy = RGBColor[0.16, 0.28, 0.46], amber = RGBColor[0.80, 0.50, \
0.18], ink = GrayLevel[0.18]},
 bx = Function[{x, lbl, guts}, {
    {GrayLevel[0.14], EdgeForm[{GrayLevel[0.5], Thickness[0.004]}],
     Rectangle[{x - 0.95, -0.8}, {x + 0.95, 0.8}]}, guts,
    White, Text[Style[lbl, 8, FontFamily -> \"Helvetica\", Bold], {x, \
0.6}]}];
 Graphics[{
   bx[-2.4, \"interior A: genuinely quantum\",
    {Lighter[navy, 0.35], Disk[{-2.4, 0.05}, 0.16],
     White, Text[Style[\"\[Gamma]\", 13, FontFamily -> \"Helvetica\"], {-2.4, \
0.05}],
     GrayLevel[0.85], Text[Style[\"single photon\", 8, FontFamily -> \
\"Helvetica\"], {-2.4, -0.45}]}],
   bx[2.4, \"interior B: classical light\",
    {amber, Thickness[0.018],
     Line[{{1.95, 0.3}, {2.85, -0.25}}], Line[{{1.95, -0.25}, {2.85, 0.3}}],
     GrayLevel[0.85], Text[Style[\"intensity optics\", 8, FontFamily -> \
\"Helvetica\"], {2.4, -0.55}]}],
   Arrowheads[0.03], GrayLevel[0.5],
   Arrow[{{-2.4, 1.5}, {-2.4, 0.85}}], Arrow[{{2.4, 1.5}, {2.4, 0.85}}],
   ink, Text[Style[\"same measurement in\", 9, FontFamily -> \"Helvetica\"], \
{0, 1.4}],
   GrayLevel[0.5], Arrow[{{-2.4, -0.85}, {-2.4, -1.5}}], Arrow[{{2.4, -0.85}, \
{2.4, -1.5}}],
   ink, Text[Style[\"identical click statistics out \[LongDash] can you tell \
which?\", 10, Bold, FontFamily -> \"Helvetica\"], {0, -1.75}]
   }, ImageSize -> 480, PlotRange -> {{-3.9, 3.9}, {-2.0, 1.6}}]
]\
\>", "Input",
 CellOpen->False,
 CellLabel->
  "In[737]:=",ExpressionUUID->"9d5781e3-a59b-49fe-b13b-0c53aa3a9804"],

Cell[BoxData[
 GraphicsBox[{{
    {GrayLevel[0.14], EdgeForm[{GrayLevel[0.5], Thickness[0.004]}], 
     RectangleBox[{-3.3499999999999996, -0.8}, {-1.45, 0.8}]}, {
     {RGBColor[0.45399999999999996`, 0.532, 0.649], 
      DiskBox[{-2.4, 0.05}, 0.16]}, 
     {GrayLevel[1], InsetBox[
       StyleBox["\<\"\[Gamma]\"\>",
        StripOnInput->False,
        FontFamily->"Helvetica",
        FontSize->13], {-2.4, 0.05}]}, 
     {GrayLevel[0.85], InsetBox[
       StyleBox["\<\"single photon\"\>",
        StripOnInput->False,
        FontFamily->"Helvetica",
        FontSize->8], {-2.4, -0.45}]}}, 
    {GrayLevel[1], InsetBox[
      StyleBox["\<\"interior A: genuinely quantum\"\>",
       StripOnInput->False,
       FontFamily->"Helvetica",
       FontSize->8,
       FontWeight->Bold], {-2.4, 0.6}]}}, {
    {GrayLevel[0.14], EdgeForm[{GrayLevel[0.5], Thickness[0.004]}], 
     RectangleBox[{1.45, -0.8}, {3.3499999999999996, 0.8}]}, 
    {RGBColor[0.8, 0.5, 0.18], Thickness[0.018], 
     LineBox[{{1.95, 0.3}, {2.85, -0.25}}], 
     LineBox[{{1.95, -0.25}, {2.85, 0.3}}], 
     {GrayLevel[0.85], InsetBox[
       StyleBox["\<\"intensity optics\"\>",
        StripOnInput->False,
        FontFamily->"Helvetica",
        FontSize->8], {2.4, -0.55}]}}, 
    {GrayLevel[1], InsetBox[
      StyleBox["\<\"interior B: classical light\"\>",
       StripOnInput->False,
       FontFamily->"Helvetica",
       FontSize->8,
       FontWeight->Bold], {2.4, 0.6}]}}, 
   {GrayLevel[0.5], Arrowheads[0.03], ArrowBox[{{-2.4, 1.5}, {-2.4, 0.85}}], 
    ArrowBox[{{2.4, 1.5}, {2.4, 0.85}}], 
    {GrayLevel[0.18], InsetBox[
      StyleBox["\<\"same measurement in\"\>",
       StripOnInput->False,
       FontFamily->"Helvetica",
       FontSize->9], {0, 1.4}]}, 
    {GrayLevel[0.5], ArrowBox[{{-2.4, -0.85}, {-2.4, -1.5}}], 
     ArrowBox[{{2.4, -0.85}, {2.4, -1.5}}]}, 
    {GrayLevel[0.18], InsetBox[
      StyleBox["\<\"identical click statistics out \[LongDash] can you tell \
which?\"\>",
       StripOnInput->False,
       FontFamily->"Helvetica",
       FontSize->10,
       FontWeight->Bold], {0, -1.75}]}}},
  ImageSize->480,
  PlotRange->{{-3.9, 3.9}, {-2., 1.6}}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->
  "Out[737]=",ExpressionUUID->"2c9a2e39-de18-4785-810a-c0218db05556"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
The rest of the essay is the sustained attempt to tell A from B \[LongDash] \
first with statistics, then, where statistics provably cannot, with geometry. \
To do that cleanly we need the simplest possible box where A and B already \
differ at all.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"776b3fb1-8cab-d84b-a554-85e3bd17b0c0"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Stage 1 \[LongDash] The Atom: the KCBS Pentagon", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"0155e221-72ef-2740-8036-f6fc468288cb"],

Cell["\<\
You do not want a complicated device to study this; you want the smallest one \
where 'quantum' and 'classical' already come apart. That object is the KCBS \
pentagon: five measurements arranged so each one is ever only compared with \
its two neighbours [3]. Joining mutually-exclusive measurements by an edge \
draws exactly a five-cycle.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"56e689ba-6ae8-c34a-acd9-162343ed4e8f"],

Cell["\<\
The exclusivity graph of the five KCBS events is the five-cycle itself:\
\>", "CodeText",ExpressionUUID->"2663e832-b2fc-7d4e-ade4-25d69a5b0355"],

Cell["\<\
Labeled[
 Graph[CycleGraph[5],
  VertexLabels -> Thread[Range[5] -> (Style[#, GrayLevel[0.2], Bold, \
FontFamily -> \"Helvetica\", 12] & /@ {\"P0\", \"P1\", \"P2\", \"P3\", \
\"P4\"})],
  VertexSize -> Medium, VertexStyle -> RGBColor[0.16, 0.28, 0.46],
  EdgeStyle -> Directive[GrayLevel[0.72], Thickness[0.008]],
  GraphLayout -> \"CircularEmbedding\", ImageSize -> 250],
 Style[\"Each measurement excludes only its two neighbours\", FontFamily -> \
\"Helvetica\", 10, GrayLevel[0.35]], Bottom]\
\>", "Input",
 CellOpen->False,
 CellLabel->
  "In[738]:=",ExpressionUUID->"7cfb722c-7d29-4383-8cdc-0515f84e0384"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TemplateBox[{"\[Placeholder]", 
   StyleBox[
   "\"Each measurement excludes only its two neighbours\"", FontFamily -> 
    "Helvetica", 10, 
    GrayLevel[0.35], StripOnInput -> False]},
  "Labeled",
  DisplayFunction->(GridBox[{{
      TagBox[
       ItemBox[
        PaneBox[
         TagBox[#, "SkipImageSizeLevel"], Alignment -> {Center, Baseline}, 
         BaselinePosition -> Baseline], DefaultBaseStyle -> "Labeled"], 
       "SkipImageSizeLevel"]}, {
      ItemBox[#2, DefaultBaseStyle -> "LabeledLabel"]}}, 
    GridBoxAlignment -> {"Columns" -> {{Center}}, "Rows" -> {{Center}}}, 
    AutoDelete -> False, 
    GridBoxItemSize -> {"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}}, 
    BaselinePosition -> {1, 1}]& ),
  InterpretationFunction->(RowBox[{"Labeled", "[", 
     RowBox[{#, ",", #2, ",", "Bottom", ",", 
       RowBox[{"{", "}"}]}], "]"}]& )]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.993084895275856*^9, 
  3.993084909462036*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"3def4cd4-d83e-4a6a-a0da-\
1fe1964313ee"],

Cell["\<\
Why five, and not three or four? A triangle fails by Specker's obstruction: \
three mutually orthogonal directions in three dimensions form a single joint \
context, so classical equals quantum and there is no gap to exploit. Even \
cycles fail too \[LongDash] they admit a full noncontextual saturation. Odd, \
and at least five, is what is needed for the classical bound to strictly \
undershoot the quantum one. The pentagon is the smallest usable cycle: the \
hydrogen atom of contextuality. Watch where the quantum value sits, \
proportionally, as the cycle grows:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2b61afdf-eaad-cf4d-8c63-f4c0bd4befd8"],

Cell["\<\
Drag n from 3 to 17: even cycles never open a gap, odd cycles \[GreaterEqual] \
5 do \[LongDash] the right panel tracks the gap across every n:\
\>", "CodeText",ExpressionUUID->"b65a6dea-1fb7-a047-9c54-2ffa58efe9d4"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Manipulate[
 Module[{a = Floor[n/2], th, as = n/2, navy = RGBColor[0.16, 0.28, 0.46],
    amber = RGBColor[0.80, 0.50, 0.18], gray = GrayLevel[0.6],
    gaps = {{3, 0.}, {4, 0.}, {5, 0.2361}, {6, 0.}, {7, 0.3177}, {8, 0.}, {9, \
0.3601},
       {10, 0.}, {11, 0.3863}, {12, 0.}, {13, 0.4042}, {14, 0.}, {15, \
0.4171}, {16, 0.}, {17, 0.4270}}},
  th = If[OddQ[n], N[n Cos[Pi/n]/(1 + Cos[Pi/n])], n/2];
  Row[{
    Graph[CycleGraph[n],
     VertexStyle -> If[OddQ[n] && n >= 5, navy, gray],
     EdgeStyle -> GrayLevel[0.7],
     VertexSize -> 0.3,
     GraphLayout -> \"CircularEmbedding\", ImageSize -> 160,
     PlotLabel -> Style[\"C\" <> ToString[n], FontFamily -> \"Helvetica\", \
12, GrayLevel[0.2]]],
    BarChart[{a, th, as}, ChartLabels -> Placed[Style[#, FontFamily -> \
\"Helvetica\", 9, GrayLevel[0.3]] & /@ {\"classical\", \"quantum\", \"ceiling\
\"}, Axis],
     ChartStyle -> {gray, navy, amber},
     PlotRange -> {0, n/2 + 0.6}, ImageSize -> 205, ImagePadding -> {{30, 8}, \
{34, 26}},
     LabelStyle -> Directive[FontFamily -> \"Helvetica\", 9, GrayLevel[0.3]],
     PlotLabel -> Style[Row[{\"gap \[Theta]-\[Alpha] = \", NumberForm[th - a, \
{4, 3}]}], FontFamily -> \"Helvetica\", 10, GrayLevel[0.25]]],
    Show[
     ListPlot[gaps, Filling -> Axis, PlotStyle -> navy, FillingStyle -> \
Opacity[0.15, navy],
      PlotRange -> {{2.5, 17.5}, {-0.04, 0.5}}, AxesLabel -> {Style[\"n\", \
FontFamily -> \"Helvetica\", 10], Style[\"gap\", FontFamily -> \"Helvetica\", \
10]},
      LabelStyle -> Directive[FontFamily -> \"Helvetica\", 9, \
GrayLevel[0.3]],
      ImageSize -> 235, ImagePadding -> {{34, 8}, {26, 16}}, GridLines -> \
Automatic,
      GridLinesStyle -> Directive[GrayLevel[0.9]]],
     Graphics[{amber, PointSize[0.035], Point[{n, th - a}]}]]
    }, Spacer[10]]],
 {{n, 5, \"cycle size n  (3 to 17)\"}, 3, 17, 1, Appearance -> \"Labeled\"},
 ControlPlacement -> Bottom]\
\>", "Input",
 Evaluatable->False,
 CellOpen->False,
 CellLabel->
  "In[739]:=",ExpressionUUID->"ee3c3aa6-003a-4956-8692-208ebf9f3578"],

