Cell["\<\
Verifying such a resource has two regimes, and it is worth being honest about \
both. The dense many-body approach is exact but explodes: a single pentagon's \
multi-qubit algebra already fills dimension 1023 = 4\:2075 - 1, and eight \
blocks would need on the order of a hundred gigabytes. The sparse stabilizer \
path sidesteps that and scales:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e8e635da-4db8-754c-ae22-8782f7b0a024"],

Cell["\<\
Two regimes for verifying the cluster \[LongDash] the exact one caps out, the \
sparse one scales:\
\>", "CodeText",ExpressionUUID->"076d0ea8-30df-f146-9ba0-0a0ad12b8918"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Module[{green = RGBColor[0.24, 0.55, 0.36], amber = RGBColor[0.80, 0.50, 0.18],
   navy = RGBColor[0.16, 0.28, 0.46], ink = GrayLevel[0.18], dot, g},
 dot[c_] := Style[\"\[FilledCircle] \", c, 13];
 g = Grid[{
    {Style[\"regime\", White, Bold, 11, FontFamily -> \"Helvetica\"],
     Style[\"reach\", White, Bold, 11, FontFamily -> \"Helvetica\"]},
    {Row[{dot[amber], \"dense many-body DLA (exact)\"}],
     \"1 pentagon \[RightArrow] dim 1023 = 4\:2075-1;  8 blocks \[TildeEqual] \
137 GiB \[RightArrow] infeasible\"},
    {Row[{dot[green], \"sparse stabilizer path\"}],
     \"structure verified to 27,000,000 qubits / 9,000,000 pentagons in \
\[TildeEqual] 312 s\"}
    },
   Background -> {None, {navy, White, GrayLevel[0.965]}},
   Frame -> None,
   Dividers -> {None, {2 -> Directive[GrayLevel[0.8], Thin]}},
   Alignment -> Left,
   ItemStyle -> Directive[FontFamily -> \"Helvetica\", 11, ink],
   Spacings -> {2.2, 1.8}, ItemSize -> {{22, 55}, Automatic}];
 Framed[g, FrameStyle -> None, FrameMargins -> {{0, 0}, {8, 0}}, Background \
-> White]
]\
\>", "Input",
 CellOpen->False,
 CellLabel->
  "In[795]:=",ExpressionUUID->"19f0ec9a-f61e-4a5d-a5a5-f7b609bc2e7f"],

